debar"><abbr title="View this template">v</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-talk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Chinese_characters_sidebar" title="Template talk:Chinese characters sidebar"><abbr title="Discuss this template">t</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-edit"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:Chinese_characters_sidebar" title="Special:EditPage/Template:Chinese characters sidebar"><abbr title="Edit this template">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwEg">A <b id="mwEw">radical</b> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_language" title="Chinese language" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zh","href":"./Template:Zh"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"部首"},"p":{"wt":"bùshǒu"},"l":{"wt":"section header"}},"i":0}}]}'>Chinese</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt14">:</span><span about="#mwt14"> </span><span lang="zh" about="#mwt14"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>部首</span><span about="#mwt14">; </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinyin" title="Pinyin" about="#mwt14">pinyin</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt14">:</span><span about="#mwt14"> </span><i about="#mwt14"><span lang="zh-Latn">bùshǒu</span></i><span about="#mwt14">; </span><abbr title="Literal translation" about="#mwt14"><small>lit.</small></abbr><span about="#mwt14"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt14">'</span><span about="#mwt14">section header</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt14">'</span>), or <b id="mwFQ">indexing component</b>, is a visually prominent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_character_components" title="Chinese character components" id="mwFg">component</a> of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_character" title="Chinese character" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFw">Chinese character</a> under which the character is traditionally listed in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_dictionary" title="Chinese dictionary" id="mwGA">Chinese dictionary</a>. The radical for a character is typically a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_component" title="Semantic component" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGQ">semantic component</a>, but it can also be another structural component or an artificially extracted portion of the character. In some cases, the original semantic or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phonology" title="Phonology" id="mwGg">phonological</a> connection has become obscure, owing to changes in the meaning or pronunciation of the character over time.</p>

<p id="mwGw">The use of the English term <i id="mwHA">radical</i> is based on an analogy between the structure of Chinese characters and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflection" title="Inflection" id="mwHQ">inflection</a> of words in European languages.<sup about="#mwt15" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"As [[Léon Wieger]] explains:\n{{blockquote|The inflected words of European languages are decomposed into &apos;&apos;radical&apos;&apos; and &apos;&apos;termination&apos;&apos;. The radical gives the meaning; the termination indicates case, time, mood. The first sinologists applied those grammatical terms belonging to inflected languages, to the Chinese language which is not an inflected one.{{sfn|Wieger|1927|p=14}}}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">[</span>a<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Radicals are also sometimes called <i id="mwIg">classifiers</i>, but this name is more commonly applied to the grammatical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_classifier" title="Chinese classifier" id="mwIw">measure words</a> in Chinese.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201334_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWilkinson201334"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201334-3"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wilkinson"},"2":{"wt":"2013"},"p":{"wt":"34"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201334-3" id="mwJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwKA" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwKQ" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_radicals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwKg">In the earliest Chinese dictionaries, such as the <i id="mwKw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erya" title="Erya" id="mwLA">Erya</a></i> (3rd century<span class="nowrap" about="#mwt26" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nbs","href":"./Template:Nbs"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span>BC), characters were grouped together in broad semantic categories.
Because the vast majority of characters are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phono-semantic" title="Phono-semantic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLg">phono-semantic</a> compounds, combining a semantic component with a phonetic component, each semantic component tended to recur within a particular section of the dictionary. In the 2nd century<span class="nowrap" about="#mwt27" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nbs","href":"./Template:Nbs"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span>AD, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwMA">Han dynasty</a> scholar <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xu_Shen" title="Xu Shen" id="mwMQ">Xu Shen</a> organized his etymological dictionary <i id="mwMg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shuowen_Jiezi" title="Shuowen Jiezi" id="mwMw">Shuowen Jiezi</a></i> by selecting 540 recurring graphic elements he called <i about="#mwt28" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhp","href":"./Template:Zhp"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"bù"},"c":{"wt":"部"},"tr":{"wt":"categories"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh-Latn">bù</span></i><span about="#mwt28"> (</span><span lang="zh" about="#mwt28"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>部</span><span about="#mwt28">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt28">"</span><span about="#mwt28">categories</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt28">"</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt28">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wilkinson"},"2":{"wt":"2013"},"p":{"wt":"74"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374-4" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup> Most were common semantic components, but they also included shared graphic elements such as a dot or horizontal stroke. Some were even artificially extracted groups of strokes, termed "glyphs" by Serruys,<sup about="#mwt35" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPA">]</span></span></a></sup> which never had an independent existence other than being listed in <i id="mwPQ">Shuowen</i>. Each character was listed under only one element, which is then referred to as the radical for that character. For example, characters containing <span lang="zh" about="#mwt32" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwPg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"女"},"p":{"wt":"nǚ"},"tr":{"wt":"female"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>女</span><span about="#mwt32">; </span><i about="#mwt32"><span lang="zh-Latn">nǚ</span></i><span about="#mwt32">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt32">"</span><span about="#mwt32">female</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt32">"</span> or <span lang="zh" about="#mwt33" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwPw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"木"},"p":{"wt":"mù"},"tr":{"wt":"tree, wood"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>木</span><span about="#mwt33">; </span><i about="#mwt33"><span lang="zh-Latn">mù</span></i><span about="#mwt33">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt33">"</span><span about="#mwt33">tree, wood</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt33">"</span> are often grouped together in the sections for those radicals.</p>

<p id="mwQA">Mei Yingzuo's 1615 dictionary <i id="mwQQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zihui" title="Zihui" id="mwQg">Zihui</a></i> made two further innovations. He reduced the list of radicals to 214 and arranged characters under each radical in increasing order of the number of additional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stroke_(CJK_character)" title="Stroke (CJK character)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwQw">strokes</a>—the radical-and-stroke method still used in the vast majority of present-day Chinese dictionaries. These innovations were also adopted by the more famous <i id="mwRA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangxi_Dictionary" title="Kangxi Dictionary" id="mwRQ">Kangxi Dictionary</a></i> of 1716. Thus the standard 214 radicals introduced in the <i id="mwRg">Zihui</i> are usually known as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangxi_radical" title="Kangxi radical" class="mw-redirect" id="mwRw">Kangxi radicals</a>. These were first called <i about="#mwt36" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwSA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhp","href":"./Template:Zhp"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"bùshǒu"},"c":{"wt":"部首"},"tr":{"wt":"section header"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh-Latn">bùshǒu</span></i><span about="#mwt36"> (</span><span lang="zh" about="#mwt36"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>部首</span><span about="#mwt36">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt36">"</span><span about="#mwt36">section header</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt36">"</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt36">)</span> in the <i id="mwSQ">Kangxi Dictionary</i>.<sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374_4-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wilkinson"},"2":{"wt":"2013"},"p":{"wt":"74"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilkinson201374-4" id="mwSg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Although there is some variation in such lists – depending primarily on what secondary radicals are also indexed – these canonical 214 radicals of the <i id="mwTg">Kangxi Dictionary</i> still serve as the basis for most modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_dictionaries" title="Chinese dictionaries" class="mw-redirect" id="mwTw">Chinese dictionaries</a>. Some of the graphically similar radicals are combined in many dictionaries, such as <span lang="zh" about="#mwt40" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"月"},"p":{"wt":"yuè"},"tr":{"wt":"moon"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>月</span><span about="#mwt40">; </span><i about="#mwt40"><span lang="zh-Latn">yuè</span></i><span about="#mwt40">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt40">"</span><span about="#mwt40">moon</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt40">"</span> and the <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt41" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"月"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">月</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt41" id="mwUg"/> form (<span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt42" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"⺼"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">⺼</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt42" id="mwVA"/>) of <span lang="zh" about="#mwt43" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwVQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"肉"},"p":{"wt":"ròu"},"tr":{"wt":"meat, flesh"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>肉</span><span about="#mwt43">; </span><i about="#mwt43"><span lang="zh-Latn">ròu</span></i><span about="#mwt43">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt43">"</span><span about="#mwt43">meat, flesh</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt43">"</span>.</p>

<p id="mwVg">After the writing system reform in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainland_China" title="Mainland China" id="mwVw">mainland China</a>, the traditional set of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangxi_radicals" title="Kangxi radicals" id="mwWA">Kangxi radicals</a> became unsuitable for indexing Simplified Chinese characters. In 1983, the Committee for Reforming the Chinese Written Language and the State Administration of Publication of China published <i id="mwWQ">The Table of Unified Indexing Chinese Character Components (Draft)</i> (<span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt44" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwWg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"汉字统一部首表（草案）"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">汉字统一部首表（草案）</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt44" id="mwWw"/>).<sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-6" id="mwXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2009, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Education_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China" title="Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYA">Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Language_Work_Committee" title="State Language Work Committee" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYQ">State Language Work Committee</a> issued <i id="mwYg">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Table_of_Indexing_Chinese_Character_Components" title="Table of Indexing Chinese Character Components" id="mwYw">Table of Indexing Chinese Character Components</a></i> (GF 0011-2009 <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt45" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwZA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"汉字部首表"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">汉字部首表</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt45" id="mwZQ"/>), which includes 201 principal indexing components and 100 associated indexing components.<sup about="#mwt52" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In China's normative documents, "radical" is defined as any component or <i id="mwag">pianpang</i> (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt46" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwaw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"偏旁"},"p":{"wt":"piānpáng"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>偏旁</span><span about="#mwt46">; </span><i about="#mwt46" id="mwbA"><span lang="zh-Latn">piānpáng</span></i>) of Chinese characters, while <i id="mwbQ">bushou</i> is translated as "indexing component".<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Identifying_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Identifying"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Identifying-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Identifying-8" id="mwbg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcA">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwcg" aria-labelledby="Shape_and_position"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Shape_and_position">Shape and position</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_radicals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Shape and position"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwcw">Radicals may appear in any position in a character. For example, <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt55" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwdA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"女"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">女</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt55" id="mwdQ"/> appears on the left side in the characters <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt56" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwdg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"姐, 媽, 她, 好"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">姐, 媽, 她, 好</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt56" id="mwdw"/> and <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt57" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"姓"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">姓</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt57" id="mweQ"/>, but it appears at the bottom in <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt58" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"妾"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">妾</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt58" id="mwew"/>. Semantic components tend to appear on the top or on the left side of the character, and phonetic components on the right side or at the bottom.<sup about="#mwt59" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChan2013_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEChan2013"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChan2013-9"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Chan"},"2":{"wt":"2013"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChan2013-9" id="mwfA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">]</span></span></a></sup> These are loose rules, however, and exceptions are plenty. Sometimes, the radical may span more than one side, as in <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt62" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"園"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">園</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt62" id="mwgQ"/> = <span lang="zh" about="#mwt63" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"囗"},"tr":{"wt":"enclosure"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>囗</span><span about="#mwt63">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt63">"</span><span about="#mwt63">enclosure</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt63">"</span> + <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt64" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"袁"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">袁</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt64" id="mwhA"/>, or <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt65" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwhQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"街"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">街</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt65" id="mwhg"/> = <span lang="zh" about="#mwt66" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwhw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"行"},"tr":{"wt":"go, movement"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>行</span><span about="#mwt66">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt66">"</span><span about="#mwt66">go, movement</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt66">"</span> + <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt67" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwiA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"圭"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">圭</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt67" id="mwiQ"/>. More complicated combinations exist, such as <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt68" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwig" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"勝"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">勝</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt68" id="mwiw"/> = <span lang="zh" about="#mwt69" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwjA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"力"},"tr":{"wt":"strength"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>力</span><span about="#mwt69">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt69">"</span><span about="#mwt69">strength</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt69">"</span> + <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt70" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwjQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"朕"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">朕</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt70" id="mwjg"/>—the radical is in the lower-right quadrant.</p>

<p id="mwjw">In many characters, the components (including radicals) are distorted or modified to fit into a block with other elements. They may be narrowed, shortened, or have different shapes entirely. Changes in shape, rather than simple distortion, may result in fewer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_character_strokes" title="Chinese character strokes" id="mwkA">strokes</a>. In some cases, combinations may have alternates. The shape of the component can depend on its placement with other elements in the character.</p>

<p id="mwkQ">The shape <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt71" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwkg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"[[阝]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/阝" title="阝">阝</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt71" id="mwkw"/> is indexed as two different radicals depending on where it appears in the character. Placed on the right, as in <i id="mwlA">du</i> (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt72" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwlQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"都"},"p":{"wt":"dū"},"tr":{"wt":"metropolis"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>都</span><span about="#mwt72">; </span><i about="#mwt72"><span lang="zh-Latn">dū</span></i><span about="#mwt72">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt72">"</span><span about="#mwt72">metropolis</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt72">"</span>) (also read as <i about="#mwt73" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwlg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"dōu"},"tr":{"wt":"all"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh-Latn">dōu</span></i><span about="#mwt73">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt73">"</span><span about="#mwt73">all</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt73">"</span>), it represents an abbreviated form of <i id="mwlw">yi</i> (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt74" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwmA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"邑"},"p":{"wt":"yì"},"tr":{"wt":"city"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>邑</span><span about="#mwt74">; </span><i about="#mwt74"><span lang="zh-Latn">yì</span></i><span about="#mwt74">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt74">"</span><span about="#mwt74">city</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt74">"</span>). Placed on the left, as in <i id="mwmQ">lu</i> (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt75" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwmg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"陸"},"p":{"wt":"lù"},"tr":{"wt":"land"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>陸</span><span about="#mwt75">; </span><i about="#mwt75"><span lang="zh-Latn">lù</span></i><span about="#mwt75">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt75">"</span><span about="#mwt75">land</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt75">"</span>), it represents an abbreviated radical form of <i id="mwmw">fu</i> (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt76" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwnA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"阜"},"p":{"wt":"fù"},"tr":{"wt":"mound, hill"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>阜</span><span about="#mwt76">; </span><i about="#mwt76"><span lang="zh-Latn">fù</span></i><span about="#mwt76">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt76">"</span><span about="#mwt76">mound, hill</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt76">"</span>).</p>

<p id="mwnQ">Some of the most important variant combining forms (besides <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt77" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwng" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"邑"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">邑</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt77" id="mwnw"/> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt78" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwoA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"阝"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">阝</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt78" id="mwoQ"/> and <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt79" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwog" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"阜"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">阜</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt79" id="mwow"/> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt80" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwpA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"阝"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">阝</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt80" id="mwpQ"/>per the above) are:</p>
<ul id="mwpg"><li id="mwpw"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt81" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwqA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"刀"},"tr":{"wt":"knife"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>刀</span><span about="#mwt81">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt81">"</span><span about="#mwt81">knife</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt81">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt82" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwqQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"刂"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">刂</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt82" id="mwqg"/> when placed to the right of other elements:
<ul id="mwqw"><li id="mwrA">examples: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt83" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwrQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"分, 召 ~ 刖"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">分, 召 ~ 刖</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt83" id="mwrg"/></li>
<li id="mwrw">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt84" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwsA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"切"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">切</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt84" id="mwsQ"/></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwsg"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt85" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwsw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"人"},"tr":{"wt":"man"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>人</span><span about="#mwt85">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt85">"</span><span about="#mwt85">man</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt85">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt86" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwtA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"亻"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">亻</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt86" id="mwtQ"/> on the left:
<ul id="mwtg"><li id="mwtw"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt87" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwuA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"囚, 仄, 坐 ~ 他"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">囚, 仄, 坐 ~ 他</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt87" id="mwuQ"/></li>
<li id="mwug">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt88" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwuw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"从"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">从</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt88" id="mwvA"/></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwvQ"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt89" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"心"},"tr":{"wt":"heart"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>心</span><span about="#mwt89">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt89">"</span><span about="#mwt89">heart</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt89">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt90" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"忄"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">忄</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt90" id="mwwA"/> on the left:
<ul id="mwwQ"><li id="mwwg"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt91" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwww" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"杺, 您, 恭* ~ 快"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">杺, 您, 恭* ~ 快</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt91" id="mwxA"/></li></ul></li></ul>
<dl id="mwxQ"><dd id="mwxg"><small id="mwxw">(*) <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt92" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwyA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"心"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">心</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt92" id="mwyQ"/> occasionally becomes <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt93" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwyg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"⺗"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">⺗</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt93" id="mwyw"/> when written at the foot of a character.</small></dd></dl>
<ul id="mwzA"><li id="mwzQ"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt94" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwzg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"手"},"tr":{"wt":"hand"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>手</span><span about="#mwt94">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt94">"</span><span about="#mwt94">hand</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt94">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt95" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwzw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"扌"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">扌</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt95" id="mw0A"/> on the left:
<ul id="mw0Q"><li id="mw0g"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt96" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw0w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"杽, 拏, 掱 ~ 扡"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">杽, 拏, 掱 ~ 扡</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt96" id="mw1A"/></li>
<li id="mw1Q">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt97" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw1g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"拜"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">拜</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt97" id="mw1w"/></li></ul></li>
<li id="mw2A"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt98" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw2Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"水"},"tr":{"wt":"water"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>水</span><span about="#mwt98">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt98">"</span><span about="#mwt98">water</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt98">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt99" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw2g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"氵"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">氵</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt99" id="mw2w"/> on the left:
<ul id="mw3A"><li id="mw3Q"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt100" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw3g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"汆, 呇, 沊 ~ 池"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">汆, 呇, 沊 ~ 池</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt100" id="mw3w"/></li>
<li id="mw4A">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt101" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw4Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"沝"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">沝</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt101" id="mw4g"/></li></ul></li>
<li id="mw4w"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt102" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw5A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"火"},"tr":{"wt":"fire"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>火</span><span about="#mwt102">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt102">"</span><span about="#mwt102">fire</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt102">"</span> → 灬 at the bottom:
<ul id="mw5Q"><li id="mw5g"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt103" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw5w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"伙, 秋, 灱 ~ 黑"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">伙, 秋, 灱 ~ 黑</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt103" id="mw6A"/></li>
<li id="mw6Q">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt104" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw6g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"災"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">災</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt104" id="mw6w"/></li></ul></li>
<li id="mw7A"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt105" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw7Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"犬"},"tr":{"wt":"dog"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>犬</span><span about="#mwt105">; </span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt105">"</span><span about="#mwt105">dog</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt105">"</span> → <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt106" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw7g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"犭"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">犭</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt106" id="mw7w"/> on the left:
<ul id="mw8A"><li id="mw8Q"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt107" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw8g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"伏, 状 ~ 狙"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">伏, 状 ~ 狙</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt107" id="mw8w"/></li>
<li id="mw9A">counter-example: <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt108" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw9Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"㹜"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">㹜</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt108" id="mw9g"/></li></ul></li></ul>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mw9w" aria-labelledby="Semantic_components"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Semantic_components">Semantic components</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_radicals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Semantic components"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt109" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw-A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Determinative"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt110" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt109" id="mw-Q">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Determinative" title="Determinative">Determinative</a></div>
<p id="mw-g">Over 80% of Chinese characters are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phono-semantic" title="Phono-semantic" class="mw-redirect" id="mw-w">phono-semantic</a> compounds (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt111" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw_A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"linktext","href":"./Template:Linktext"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"zh"},"1":{"wt":"形聲字"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/形聲字#Chinese" title="wikt:形聲字" class="extiw">形聲字</a></span>):<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELiu2010_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELiu2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELiu2010-10"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Liu"},"2":{"wt":"2010"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELiu2010-10" id="mw_Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_w">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQA">]</span></span></a></sup> a semantic component gives a broad category of meaning, while a phonetic component suggests the sound. Usually, the radical is the semantic component.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWoon1987148_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWoon1987148"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWoon1987148-11"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Woon"},"2":{"wt":"1987"},"p":{"wt":"148"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWoon1987148-11" id="mwAQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQU">Thus, although some authors use the term <i id="mwAQY">radical</i> for semantic components (<span lang="zh" about="#mwt118" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAQc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"義符"},"p":{"wt":"yìfú"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>義符</span><span about="#mwt118">; </span><i about="#mwt118" id="mwAQg"><span lang="zh-Latn">yìfú</span></i>),<sup about="#mwt119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wieger uses the terms \"keys of the dictionary\" and \"the 214 keys of K&apos;ang-hsi\" for {{zhi|c=部首|p=bùshǒu}}, reserving the term \"radical\" for any element bearing meaning.{{sfn|Wieger|1927|p=14}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-12" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwAQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQs">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTERamsey1987136–137_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTERamsey1987136–137"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERamsey1987136–137-13"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Ramsey"},"2":{"wt":"1987"},"pp":{"wt":"136–137"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTERamsey1987136–137-13" id="mwAQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ8">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARA">]</span></span></a></sup> others distinguish the latter as <i id="mwARE">determinatives</i><sup about="#mwt128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBoltz199467–68_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBoltz199467–68"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBoltz199467–68-14"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Boltz"},"2":{"wt":"1994"},"pp":{"wt":"67–68"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBoltz199467–68-14" id="mwARI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARQ">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARU">]</span></span></a></sup> or <i id="mwARY">significs</i><sup about="#mwt131" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENorman198862_15-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENorman198862"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENorman198862-15"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Norman"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"62"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENorman198862-15" id="mwARc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARk">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARo">]</span></span></a></sup> or by some other term.<sup about="#mwt134" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Woon gives an extensive list of the translations of {{zhi|c=義符|p=yìfú}}: semantic element, radical, determinative, signific, signifying part, significant, significant part, semantic part, meaning element, meaning part, sense-indicator, radical-determinative, lexical morpheme symbol, ideographic element, and logographic part. Among them, \"radical\" and \"ideographic\" have both been strenuously objected to as misleading.{{sfn|Woon|1987|p=291}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-17" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwARs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR0">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt140" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-19"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Professor Woon Wee Lee (1987) also explains:\n\n{{blockquote|It is important to note that the concepts of semantic element and \"section heading\" ({{zhi|c=部首|p=bùshǒu}}) are different, and should be clearly distinguished. The semantic element is parallel to the phonetic element in terms of the phonetic compound, while the section heading is a terminology of Chinese lexicography, which is a generic heading for the characters arranged in each section of a dictionary according to the system established by Xu Shen. It is the \"head\" of a section, assigned for convenience only. Thus, a section heading is usually the element common to all characters belonging to the same section. (Cf. L. Wang, 1962:1.151). The semantic elements of phonetic compounds were usually also used as section headings. However, characters in the same section are not necessarily all phonetic compounds. ...In some sections, such as {{Lang|zh|品}} pin3 \"the masses\" (S. Xu 1963:48) and {{Lang|zh|爪}} zhua3 \"a hand\" (S. Xu 1963:63), no phonetic compound is incorporated. In other words, the section heading was not commonly used as a semantic element...To sum up, the selection of a section heading is to some extent arbitrary.{{sfn|Woon|1987|pp=147–148}}}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-19" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwAR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-21" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-21"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"When an etymon (original \"root\" form of a graph, such as {{zhi|c=采|p=cǎi|tr=to pick}}, in {{zhi|c=採|p=cǎi|tr=to pick}}) is analyzed alongside the remaining element(s), it cannot be said to be playing only a phonetic role. For instance, operating under the two misconceptions that a) all characters have exactly one semantic and one phonetic part, and b) each part can only play one role, many would mistakenly dissect {{Lang|zh|採}} as comprising {{zhi|c=扌|p=shǒu|Tr=hand}} semantic and {{zhi|c=采|p=cǎi}} phonetic. However, being the original graph, it must necessarily impart its original semantic meaning (showing as it does a hand &apos;&apos;picking&apos;&apos; from a tree) as well as its sound. In the case of {{zhi|c=陷|p=xiàn}} \"pit trap; fall into\", for instance, [[Duan Yucai]] notes in his annotation of the &apos;&apos;Shuowen Jiezi&apos;&apos;&lt;ref>Duan Yucai (v.14, p.732)&lt;/ref> that the Dà Xú {{Lang|zh|大徐}} edition acknowledges that {{Lang|zh|臽}} plays the dual roles of phonetic and semantic in {{Lang|zh|陷}}, stating \"{{Lang|zh|从阝, 从臽, 臽 亦聲\".}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-21" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwASM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">[</span>e<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASc">Many radicals are artificial extractions of portions of characters, some of which are further changed when applied (such as <span lang="zh" about="#mwt154" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwASg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"亅"},"p":{"wt":"jué, juě"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>亅</span><span about="#mwt154">; </span><i about="#mwt154" id="mwASk"><span lang="zh-Latn">jué, juě</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt155" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwASo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"了"},"p":{"wt":"liǎo"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>了</span><span about="#mwt155">; </span><i about="#mwt155" id="mwASs"><span lang="zh-Latn">liǎo</span></i>), as explained by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Serruys" title="Paul Serruys" id="mwASw">Serruys</a> (1984), who therefore prefers the term "glyph" extraction rather than graphic extraction.<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-22" id="mwAS0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">]</span></span></a></sup> This is even truer of modern dictionaries, which cut radicals to less than half the number in <i id="mwATE">Shuowen</i>, at which point it becomes impossible to have enough to cover a semantic element of every character. A sample of the <i id="mwATI">Far Eastern Chinese English Dictionary</i> of mere artificial extraction of a stroke from sub-entries:</p>
<ul id="mwATM"><li id="mwATQ"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt158" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"一"},"p":{"wt":"yī"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>一</span><span about="#mwt158">; </span><i about="#mwt158" id="mwATY"><span lang="zh-Latn">yī</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt159" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"丁"},"p":{"wt":"dīng"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>丁</span><span about="#mwt159">; </span><i about="#mwt159" id="mwATg"><span lang="zh-Latn">dīng</span></i> and <span lang="zh" about="#mwt160" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"且"},"p":{"wt":"qiě"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>且</span><span about="#mwt160">; </span><i about="#mwt160" id="mwATo"><span lang="zh-Latn">qiě</span></i></li>
<li id="mwATs"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt161" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"乙"},"p":{"wt":"yǐ"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>乙</span><span about="#mwt161">; </span><i about="#mwt161" id="mwAT0"><span lang="zh-Latn">yǐ</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt162" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAT4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"九"},"p":{"wt":"jiǔ"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>九</span><span about="#mwt162">; </span><i about="#mwt162" id="mwAT8"><span lang="zh-Latn">jiǔ</span></i></li>
<li id="mwAUA"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt163" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"亅"},"p":{"wt":"jué/juě"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>亅</span><span about="#mwt163">; </span><i about="#mwt163" id="mwAUI"><span lang="zh-Latn">jué/juě</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt164" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"了"},"p":{"wt":"liǎo/le"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>了</span><span about="#mwt164">; </span><i about="#mwt164" id="mwAUQ"><span lang="zh-Latn">liǎo/le</span></i></li>
<li id="mwAUU"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt165" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"二"},"p":{"wt":"èr"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>二</span><span about="#mwt165">; </span><i about="#mwt165" id="mwAUc"><span lang="zh-Latn">èr</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt166" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"亞"},"p":{"wt":"yà/yǎ"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>亞</span><span about="#mwt166">; </span><i about="#mwt166" id="mwAUk"><span lang="zh-Latn">yà/yǎ</span></i></li>
<li id="mwAUo"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt167" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"田"},"p":{"wt":"tián"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>田</span><span about="#mwt167">; </span><i about="#mwt167" id="mwAUw"><span lang="zh-Latn">tián</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt168" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAU0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"禺"},"p":{"wt":"yù"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>禺</span><span about="#mwt168">; </span><i about="#mwt168" id="mwAU4"><span lang="zh-Latn">yù</span></i></li>
<li id="mwAU8"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt169" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAVA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"豕"},"p":{"wt":"shǐ"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>豕</span><span about="#mwt169">; </span><i about="#mwt169" id="mwAVE"><span lang="zh-Latn">shǐ</span></i> in <span lang="zh" about="#mwt170" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAVI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"zhi","href":"./Template:Zhi"},"params":{"c":{"wt":"象"},"p":{"wt":"xiàng"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text"/>象</span><span about="#mwt170">; </span><i about="#mwt170" id="mwAVM"><span lang="zh-Latn">xiàng</span></i>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwAVQ" aria-labelledby="Phonetic_components"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Phonetic_components">Phonetic components</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_radicals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Phonetic components"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAVU">Radicals sometimes play a phonetic role instead of a semantic one:</p>
<table class="wikitable sortable" id="mwAVY">
<tbody id="mwAVc"><tr id="mwAVg"><th id="mwAVk">Phonetic part</th><th id="mwAVo">pinyin</th><th id="mwAVs">meaning</th><th id="mwAVw">Character</th><th id="mwAV0">pinyin</th><th id="mwAV4">meaning</th></tr>
<tr id="mwAV8">
<td rowspan="2" id="mwAWA"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt171" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"[[臼]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/臼" title="臼" class="mw-redirect">臼</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt171" id="mwAWI"/></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwAWM"><span title="Pinyin transliteration" about="#mwt172" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"pinyin"},"3":{"wt":"jiù"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn">jiù</i></span></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwAWU">"a mortar"</td>
<td id="mwAWY"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt173" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"舅"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">舅</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt173" id="mwAWg"/></td><td id="mwAWk"><span title="Pinyin transliteration" about="#mwt174" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"pinyin"},"3":{"wt":"jiù"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn">jiù</i></span></td><td id="mwAWs">"maternal uncle"<sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwAWw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAW0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW8">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
<tr id="mwAXA">
<td id="mwAXE"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt177" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAXI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"舊"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">舊</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt177" id="mwAXM"/></td><td id="mwAXQ"><span title="Pinyin transliteration" about="#mwt178" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAXU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"pinyin"},"3":{"wt":"jiù"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn">jiù</i></span></td><td id="mwAXY">"owl; old" <sup about="#mwt181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-24" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-24" id="mwAXc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXk">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXo">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
<tr id="mwAXs">
<td id="mwAXw"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt182" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAX0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"虎"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">虎</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt182" id="mwAX4"/></td><td id="mwAX8"><span title="Pinyin transliteration" about="#mwt183" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAYA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"pinyin"},"3":{"wt":"hǔ"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn">hǔ</i></span></td><td id="mwAYE">"tiger"</td><td id="mwAYI"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt184" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAYM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"虖"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="zh">虖</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt184" id="mwAYQ"/></td><td id="mwAYU"><span title="Pinyin transliteration" about="#mwt185" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAYY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"pinyin"},"3":{"wt":"hū"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn">hū</i></span></td><td id="mwAYc">"shout"</td></tr>
<tr id="mwAYg">
